TITLE: UAOP low-level requirements: API gateway
UID: UAOP-LLR-GW
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-21
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: ../02-standards/requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Low-level requirements of the API gateway (`backend/api-gateway/src/`), written from the code as read on 2026-11-21. The gateway is the only built item on the command and telemetry paths, which is why it is the one item with requirements at this level. Design: `docs/lifecycle/06-design/lld-gateway.md`. Where the code does less than a high-level requirement asks, the gap is a problem report and the requirement here states what the code does.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Command forwarding (`routes/commands.js`)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-001
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
The command table maps exactly ARM, DISARM, MODE, RTL, TAKEOFF, LAND and MISSION_START to `COMMAND_KIND_<name>`. Lookup is by exact, case-sensitive match of the `command` field of the JSON body.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-002
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
When the lookup fails, or the body or `command` is missing, the route answers 400 with `{error: {code: "ERROR_CODE_INVALID_ARGUMENT", message}}` before any service client is obtained.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-003
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
The `SubmitCommand` request is built as: `vehicleId` from the path segment unchanged, `command` from the table, `params` from the body or an empty object, `idempotencyKey` from the `Idempotency-Key` header or an empty string.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: No check of the vehicle identifier or of `params` (PR-010).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-004
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
On a successful `SubmitCommand` the route answers 202 with `{correlation_id}`. On a call error it answers 502 with `{error: {code: "ERROR_CODE_UNAVAILABLE", message}}` carrying the error text. The call is made without a deadline.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-005
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /commands/{correlationId}` calls `GetCommandResult` with the path value and answers 200 with the `result` object, or 502 with `ERROR_CODE_UNAVAILABLE` on a call error.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-006
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
Service clients are created once per service name and target address and reused; the default target is `localhost:50051` (`UAOP_GATEWAY_GRPC_TARGET`) and the channel is not encrypted.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: A configuration property; reviewed against `grpc/client.js` and `config.js`.
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-001

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Authentication (`auth/`, `index.js`)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-007
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
The authentication step reads the `Authorization` header, requires the form `Bearer <token>`, verifies the token with HS256 and the configured secret, and looks its identifier up in the revoked list. It answers 401 with `ERROR_CODE_UNAUTHENTICATED` when the header is missing or malformed, the token is invalid or expired, or the identifier is revoked. Otherwise it attaches subject, role, organisation, token identifier and expiry to the request.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-008
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
Handlers are installed in this order: JSON body parser, health route, login and logout routes, authentication step, command routes. Only handlers after the authentication step are protected by it.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: Order of installation in `index.js`.
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: Logout is installed before the step that identifies the caller (PR-015). The WebSocket is not an HTTP handler and is not protected (PR-004).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-009
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
Tokens are signed with HS256, live `UAOP_GATEWAY_JWT_TTL_SECONDS` seconds (default 3600) and carry subject, role, organisation and a unique identifier. A role outside the six defined roles is refused at issue.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: The secret falls back to a fixed development value when the variable is unset (PR-007).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-010
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
Revoking stores the token identifier in Redis with a life equal to the token's remaining life; a remaining life of zero or less stores nothing. A stored identifier is reported as revoked.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-007

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Stream relay (`streams/websocket.js`)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-011
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
A `subscribe` message first cancels every bus subscription of the connection and clears its stream states, then for each requested telemetry category subscribes to `uaop.telemetry.v1.<vehicle>.<category>` under the stream key `telemetry.<vehicle>.<category>`, and for each requested event domain subscribes to `uaop.event.v1.<domain>.>` under `events.<domain>`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: The vehicle, category and domain strings are used unchecked (PR-004).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-012
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
Each relayed message is sent as `{stream, seq, ts, payload}`: `seq` starts at 1 and rises by 1 per relayed frame of that stream on that connection, `ts` is the gateway's clock at sending in ISO 8601, `payload` is the message bytes in base64. Nothing is sent when the socket is not open.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: `ts` is not the source time (PR-006).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-013
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
A telemetry stream with `rate_hz` greater than zero relays a message only when at least `1000 / rate_hz` milliseconds have passed since the last relayed one, and otherwise adds 1 to the stream's dropped count. A stream with no rate, or a rate of zero or less, and every event stream, relays every message.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-014
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
When a message is relayed and the stream's dropped count is above zero, the gateway first sends `{op: "gap", stream, dropped}` and sets the count to zero.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: No gap frame is sent while no further message is relayed (FMEA T4).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-015
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
From connection until close the gateway sends `{op: "heartbeat", ts}` every `UAOP_GATEWAY_WS_HEARTBEAT_MS` milliseconds (default 5000); on close it stops the timer and cancels the connection's bus subscriptions.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-GW-016
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
A client message that is not valid JSON is answered with `{op: "error", message: "invalid JSON"}`; a message whose `op` is not `subscribe` is answered with an error frame naming the operation. The connection stays open in both cases.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-GW-008

[[/SECTION]]
